      {
        "text": "A counterpoint to the rate hike is that inflation remained soft — market-based measures of inflation compensation were low and inflation was expected to stay below 2 percent near term — which is the implied concern behind Kashkari's dissent to hold rates steady. The dissent itself is the cited opposing evidence in the document.",
